Subject: State the safety property before choosing the mechanism
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Message-ID: <safety-property-historical@inkcre.acceptance>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A distributed design becomes easier to review when its safety property is
written before locks, leases, queues, or retries are chosen.  For a scheduler,
the property might be: one schedule occurrence creates at most one durable job.

That statement leaves implementation freedom while giving every proposed
mechanism a precise burden of proof.  It also exposes which failures are merely
missed opportunities and which ones corrupt authority.
